      "kind": "documentation",
      "native": {
        "id": null,
        "value": {
          "attachment": "native_docstring",
          "attachment_identity": "python:The-Interdependency/ucns:src/ucns/gonal_boundary_trace.py::function:pullback_circle_wave_trace",
          "description": "For positive integer ``d``, the circle-wave equation is preserved by\n``(theta, t) -> (d*theta, d*t)``. On an ``m``-gonal trace, only ``d mod m``\nremains in the residue action. The caller therefore supplies ``d``\nexplicitly, and this function requires ``d % m == geometry.multiplier``.",
          "fields": [],
          "format": "rest",
          "metadata_kind": "documentation",
          "summary": "Witness one explicit continuum covering above a finite modular action.",
          "text": "Witness one explicit continuum covering above a finite modular action.\n\n    For positive integer ``d``, the circle-wave equation is preserved by\n    ``(theta, t) -> (d*theta, d*t)``. On an ``m``-gonal trace, only ``d mod m``\n    remains in the residue action. The caller therefore supplies ``d``\n    explicitly, and this function requires ``d % m == geometry.multiplier``.\n    "
        }
      },
