      "kind": "documentation",
      "native": {
        "id": null,
        "value": {
          "attachment": "native_docstring",
          "attachment_identity": "python:The-Interdependency/ucns:src/ucns/ordinal_affixiation.py::<module>",
          "description": "This module remains replayable for existing receipts and non-text experiments that\nexplicitly select it. It is superseded for active Unicode text geometry by\n``ucns.unicode_gonol``. New text construction must not infer canon from the\nradius-halving law here.\n\n\nUsage:\n    carrier = Carrier(('A', 'B'), 'example-v1')\n    word = affixiate('AB', (Participant.atom(carrier, 'A'),\n                           Participant.atom(carrier, 'B')),\n                     origin='SPACE', relation='ordered', source='example:AB')\n    assert word.placement(0).radius() == Fraction(1, 4)\n\nA closed construction may be registered on another explicitly supplied carrier\nwith Participant.closed(). It is never flattened into a hash or a last-glyph\nangle. Angles are exact turns; floats are optional rendering only. Every frame\nis local. No implicit cross-frame translation, rotation, or Mobius lift is made.",
          "fields": [],
          "format": "rest",
          "metadata_kind": "documentation",
          "summary": "Historical exact local-frame ordinal affixiation, independent of language.",
          "text": "Historical exact local-frame ordinal affixiation, independent of language.\n\nThis module remains replayable for existing receipts and non-text experiments that\nexplicitly select it. It is superseded for active Unicode text geometry by\n``ucns.unicode_gonol``. New text construction must not infer canon from the\nradius-halving law here.\n\n\nUsage:\n    carrier = Carrier(('A', 'B'), 'example-v1')\n    word = affixiate('AB', (Participant.atom(carrier, 'A'),\n                           Participant.atom(carrier, 'B')),\n                     origin='SPACE', relation='ordered', source='example:AB')\n    assert word.placement(0).radius() == Fraction(1, 4)\n\nA closed construction may be registered on another explicitly supplied carrier\nwith Participant.closed(). It is never flattened into a hash or a last-glyph\nangle. Angles are exact turns; floats are optional rendering only. Every frame\nis local. No implicit cross-frame translation, rotation, or Mobius lift is made.\n"
        }
      },
